Regarding different baselines for different fonts, first the
baselineskip is primarily an issue of the document's design.
Second, so is the font. In an ideal world, use of generic styles
would be limited and specific styles would be the norm. For the
latter, there should be no  reason to specify font X or header
style Y or any of that.

Generic styles on the other hand might be well-advised to allow
setting of baselineskips from the user level somehow.

-dh

